Rule 4 (index tensor (v_3) is within the input tensor along the specified dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : tensor} |= min(v_3) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_3) ≤ shape(v_1, v_2) - 1
>>
Rule 5 (last dimension of a tensor matches first dimension of the other)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 6 (input tensor has at least one dimension)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 7 (dim parameter is valid for input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= -1 ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1
>>
Rule 8 (dim parameter is valid for input tensor when it's a tuple)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : -1 ≤ v_2[i] ∧ v_2[i] ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1
>>
Rule 9 (input tensor is not empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) > 0
>>
Rule 11 (input tensor has valid shape)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 14 (input tensor has valid dimensions with respect to shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= v_2 ≤ shape(v_1, v_2)
